# Product Requirements Document (PRD): Real-Time P2P Fraud Routing & AI Ops Copilot

Document Status: Approved for Engineering Review
Target Release: Phase 1 (P2P Transfer & Cash-Out Flows)
Owner: Product / Risk Business Analyst

---

## 1. Scope & System Boundaries

### In-Scope
- Real-time risk scoring for outbound TRANSFER and CASH_OUT transactions.
- Three-tier automated routing (Auto-Approve, Step-Up Biometric Auth, Hold for Ops Review).
- AI Investigation Copilot generating plain-text risk summaries for Fraud Ops analysts.
- Audit logging for all manual overrides and system decisions.

### Out-of-Scope
- Inbound CASH_IN transactions and routine utility BILL_PAYMENT flows (0% historical fraud rate).
- Automated permanent account bans (requires human-in-the-loop approval).

---

## 2. Functional Requirements & User Stories

### Epic 1: Real-Time Risk Scoring & Routing

#### US-1.1: Frictionless Approval for Low-Risk Transfers
As a legitimate e-wallet user, I want my routine P2P transfers to complete immediately without extra verification steps so that my payment experience remains fast.
- Acceptance Criteria:
  - GIVEN a user initiates a TRANSFER or CASH_OUT request
  - WHEN the ML Scoring Engine returns a Risk Score between 0 and 30 within 250ms
  - THEN the Core Payment Service automatically approves and settles the transaction within 1 second without prompting for additional authentication.

#### US-1.2: Step-Up Biometric Authentication for Medium-Risk Transfers
As a Risk Manager, I want suspicious transactions in the medium-risk tier to undergo biometric liveness verification so that we stop unauthorized access while allowing genuine users to self-verify.
- Acceptance Criteria:
  - GIVEN a transaction receives a Risk Score between 31 and 75
  - WHEN the routing engine evaluates the score
  - THEN the app displays a biometric Liveness Check prompt matched against the user's registered chip-based ID.
  - AND IF the biometric match succeeds within 3 attempts, the transaction status updates to APPROVED and funds are released.
  - AND IF the biometric check fails 3 consecutive times, the transaction is marked FAILED, the session is locked for 15 minutes, and a security alert is sent to the user.

#### US-1.3: Transaction Hold & Escalation for High-Risk Anomalies
As a Risk Manager, I want high-risk transfers (e.g., draining 100% balance on a new device) to be temporarily frozen so that Fraud Ops can investigate before funds leave the platform.
- Acceptance Criteria:
  - GIVEN a transaction receives a Risk Score between 76 and 100
  - WHEN the routing engine processes the result
  - THEN the transaction status is set to ON_HOLD for a maximum window of 30 minutes (funds are reserved from sender's available balance but not credited to the recipient).
  - AND a high-priority investigation ticket is created in the Fraud Ops Portal enriched with an AI Copilot summary.

---

### Epic 2: AI Investigation Copilot & Fraud Ops Portal

#### US-2.1: Automated Case Summarization
As a Fraud Ops Analyst, I want to see a concise 3-bullet summary of why a transaction was flagged so that I can make an approval or rejection decision in under 2 minutes.
- Acceptance Criteria:
  - GIVEN a transaction enters the ON_HOLD queue
  - WHEN the Ops Portal loads the case details
  - THEN the AI Copilot displays a structured summary highlighting top risk drivers (e.g., balance drain ratio, device change recency, velocity spikes) alongside a recommended action.
  - AND all Personally Identifiable Information (PII) is masked prior to LLM processing.

#### US-2.2: Human-in-the-Loop Decision & Audit Trail
As a Compliance Officer, I want every manual decision made by Fraud Ops to require a reason code and be permanently logged so that we maintain full regulatory auditability.
- Acceptance Criteria:
  - GIVEN a Fraud Ops Analyst reviews an ON_HOLD ticket
  - WHEN the analyst clicks either Approve or Reject
  - THEN the system requires selecting a standardized Reason Code and entering optional notes.
  - AND an immutable record is written to the Audit_Logs table capturing analyst_id, transaction_id, previous_status, new_status, ai_recommendation_followed (boolean), and timestamp.

